<!-- ═══════════════ 2. BTS DIFFERENCE ═══════════════ -->
<section class="bts-section light">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="bts-head">
      <span class="rule"></span>
      <span class="kicker">The BTS difference</span>
      <h2>Translation is not bilingual. BTS builds in both languages.</h2>
      <p>Four principles that shape every bilingual system we deliver.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="bts-pillars">
      <div class="bts-pillar">
        <span class="num">01 · DESIGNED TOGETHER</span>
        <h3>Arabic and English designed at the same time</h3>
        <p>Not English-first, Arabic-later. Every screen, every field, every label is designed in both languages from the start.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bts-pillar">
        <span class="num">02 · NATIVE RTL</span>
        <h3>Right-to-left is the layout, not an afterthought</h3>
        <p>Proper RTL reading order, mirrored layouts, right-aligned tables, RTL-aware icons and number formatting.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bts-pillar">
        <span class="num">03 · NOT JUST UI</span>
        <h3>Documents, notifications and reports too</h3>
        <p>Invoices, approvals, alerts and reports are bilingual — because your business doesn't stop at the interface.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bts-pillar">
        <span class="num">04 · ONE CODEBASE</span>
        <h3>One system, two languages, no duplication</h3>
        <p>Not two parallel platforms to maintain. One application that switches language without changing behaviour.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ═══════════════ 3. WHAT WE BUILD ═══════════════ -->
<section class="bts-section navy">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="bts-head">
      <span class="rule"></span>
      <span class="kicker">What we build</span>
      <h2>Bilingual systems for the way UK and GCC teams actually work.</h2>
      <p>Six capabilities that make bilingual delivery real — not a translation layer on top of an English product.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="bts-services">
      <div class="bts-svc">
        <h3>Arabic + English Interfaces</h3>
        <p>Dashboards, portals and applications that display in either language — with full RTL layouts, not just translated labels.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bts-svc">
        <h3>Bilingual Documents</h3>
        <p>Invoices, purchase orders, delivery notes, contracts and customs paperwork generated in Arabic, English, or both.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bts-svc">
        <h3>Notifications &amp; Alerts</h3>
        <p>WhatsApp messages, emails and system alerts that reach the right person in the language they read.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bts-svc">
        <h3>Bilingual Reporting</h3>
        <p>Dashboards and reports in both languages — same numbers, same filters, same behaviour, no duplicated data.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bts-svc">
        <h3>Language Switching</h3>
        <p>Instant language toggle that preserves state, respects user preference, and works on every device.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bts-svc">
        <h3>Localisation &amp; Formats</h3>
        <p>Dates, currency, numbers, addresses and business terminology adapted for GCC and UK usage.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ═══════════════ 4. HOW WE WORK ═══════════════ -->
<section class="bts-section light" id="how">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="bts-head">
      <span class="rule"></span>
      <span class="kicker">How we work</span>
      <h2>From the first screen to a fully bilingual system.</h2>
      <p>Three phases. Each one delivers something testable in both languages before moving to the next.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="bts-phases">
      <div class="bts-phase">
        <div class="bts-phase-num">01</div>
        <h3>Define</h3>
        <p class="bts-phase-lead">We agree what needs to be bilingual — interface, documents, notifications, reports — and define terminology, formats and RTL behaviour in both languages.</p>
        <div class="bts-phase-meta">
          <span class="bts-phase-label">Typical duration</span>
          <span class="bts-phase-value">1–2 weeks</span>
        </div>
        <div class="bts-phase-meta">
          <span class="bts-phase-label">You receive</span>
          <span class="bts-phase-value">Bilingual scope, terminology guide, RTL design specification</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="bts-phase featured">
        <div class="bts-phase-num">02</div>
        <h3>Build</h3>
        <p class="bts-phase-lead">We develop both languages in parallel. Every screen, form and message is reviewed in Arabic and English before it ships — not translated after launch.</p>
        <div class="bts-phase-meta">
          <span class="bts-phase-label">Typical duration</span>
          <span class="bts-phase-value">4–8 weeks</span>
        </div>
        <div class="bts-phase-meta">
          <span class="bts-phase-label">You receive</span>
          <span class="bts-phase-value">Working bilingual system, tested in both languages, ready for rollout</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="bts-phase">
        <div class="bts-phase-num">03</div>
        <h3>Extend</h3>
        <p class="bts-phase-lead">As your system grows — new screens, new documents, new workflows — bilingual delivery continues. Terminology, formatting and RTL patterns carry forward automatically.</p>
        <div class="bts-phase-meta">
          <span class="bts-phase-label">Typical duration</span>
          <span class="bts-phase-value">Ongoing</span>
        </div>
        <div class="bts-phase-meta">
          <span class="bts-phase-label">You receive</span>
          <span class="bts-phase-value">New bilingual features, terminology updates, ongoing review</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="bts-phases-note">A bilingual system is not two systems. It is one system that respects the language of every person who uses it.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ═══════════════ 5. UK + GCC ADVANTAGE ═══════════════ -->
<section class="bts-section navy">
  <div class="container">
